# /etc/liquidity-migration/engine.env  --  root-owned, mode 0600
#
# The Rust execution engine's unit settings. Copy this file to the path above
# on the VPS and edit it there; it is never written by a deploy.
#
# Putting this file on a host is how that host says "run the engine here". The
# deploy starts and verifies the engine only where this file and a built binary
# both exist, so a box without it is simply a box that does not run the engine.
# Deleting it (and stopping the unit) takes the engine back out of that host's
# expected topology.
#
# The credentials are NOT here: the unit loads them from
# /etc/liquidity-migration/bybit-demo.env — the fleet's demo account
# (555899665), the live demo book. The engine is that account's only writer
# since the Python order path was deleted (2026-08-14), and a live engine
# holds the account's single-writer lease. (Its first live day ran on a
# second demo account, 579580669 in bybit-quote-lab.env; nothing holds that
# lease now.)
#
# Format: strict KEY=value, one per line, no inline comments, no quotes, no
# shell expansion. systemd reads it verbatim.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. The engine's config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which strategies run, at what size, against which compiled-in venue adapter.
# There is no venue address in it and no way to put one there. The deploy does
# not write this file either; it is yours.
ENGINE_CONFIG_FILE=/etc/liquidity-migration/engine.toml


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Being watched
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The fleet's watchdog (check_fleet_liveness.py, every three minutes) reads the
# engine's heartbeat file and pages when it goes stale, cannot be read, or says
# the engine has stopped opening positions. Leave this line out and the
# watchdog says nothing about the engine at all.
#
# THIS MUST BE THE SAME PATH as `heartbeat_path` in the [engine] block of the
# config above, and nothing checks that for you: the engine reads its path from
# the config, the watchdog reads it from here. Two different paths means the
# engine writes a file nobody reads and the watchdog pages about a file nobody
# writes. If `heartbeat_path` is left out of the config the engine writes
# nothing, so leave this out too.
LIVENESS_ENGINE_HEARTBEAT_FILE=/var/lib/liquidity-migration-engine/heartbeat.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. How much it says (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset means info. Everything the engine prints goes to the journal, which is
# capped at 500M by the deploy — a debug level on a busy market fills that in
# hours and pushes out the fleet's own logs.
RUST_LOG=info
